  "reason": "Evidence: RNA encoder is the most impactful design choice (scvi_n200 yields 0.650 RNA-only vs 0.591 for pca_n2000; multimodal scvi_n200+ViT-L reaches 0.715). However, scgpt has not been tested in any experiment, leaving a significant gap in our understanding of the RNA representation space. Question: config_008 (scgpt, ViT-L, avgpool, concat) is a single-variable change from the current best (config_042: scvi_n200, ViT-L, avgpool, concat), isolating the effect of RNA encoder while holding image encoder, aggregation, and fusion constant. Why best next: The uncertainty around scgpt is the largest remaining unknown among all design dimensions. If scgpt is competitive or superior, it opens a new promising direction; if clearly inferior, we can confidently rule it out and consolidate on scvi_n200. This high-uncertainty, single-variable experiment maximizes information gain per budget unit compared to small refinements around the already-well-characterized scvi_n200+ViT-L configuration."
}

